==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nb|a la mode}}

===Etymology===
{{root|nb|ine-pro|*h₂el-}} {{root|nb|ine-pro|*med-}}
From {{bor|nb|fr|à la mode||in fashion}}, first part from {{bor|nb|fr|à la||in the [[style]] or [[manner]] of}}, short for {{l|nb|à la mode||in fashion}}, first part from {{der|nb|fr|à||to, on, in}}, from {{der|nb|frm}}, from {{der|nb|fro|a||to, towards, belonging to}}, from {{der|nb|la|ad||to, towards, up to, at}}, from {{der|nb|itc-pro|*ad||toward, to, on, up to, for}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂éd||to, at}} + middle part from {{der|nb|fr|la||the}}, from {{der|nb|frm|la||the}}, from {{der|nb|fro|la||the}}, from {{der|nb|la|illam||that, those}}, which is the accusative singular feminine of {{m|la|ille||that, those}}, from {{der|nb|itc-ola|olle||he, that}}, from {{der|nb|ine-pro|*h₂ol-no-}} or {{m|ine-pro|*h₂l̥-no-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂el-||beyond, other}}. Last part from {{der|nb|fr|mode||fashion, trend}}, from {{der|nb|frm|mode}}, from {{der|nb|fro|mode|g=f}}, from {{der|nb|la|modus|g=m||measure, manner; bound, mood}}, from {{der|nb|itc-pro|*modōs}}, from {{der|nb|ine-pro||*mod-ōs|measure}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*med-||to measure}}.

